In the C++ backend, a `match` inside another expression compiles outside of witnesses, a new array holds its element type's default value instead of uninitialized memory, `bool` and `char` default to `false` and `'D'` inside tuples and generic types, and an instance const's initializer sees the consts that the constructor assigns. In C#, Java, JavaScript, Go and Python, a lambda in a tail-recursive method compiles when a let expression in it uses `this`.
